//
// The page helpers pageNum, totalPages and chapter are described with
// <header> and <footer> below.
//
// # Document tags
//
// <document> sets up the document. Its attributes are page-size (A3, A4, A5,
// Letter or Legal, in any case, or a width and height in points such as
// "595 842"), orientation (portrait or landscape, in any case, swapping the
// page width and height as needed), margin (the page margins, in the format
// every other tag uses), lang (the catalog language) and title (the document
// info title, see Creator.SetTitle). They apply in that order whatever order they are written
// in, before the content inside the tag is drawn. The content inside renders
// as if the tag were absent and inherits the typography the tag sets (font,
// font-size, color, ...), but not lang, which only sets the catalog language.
// A template has at most one <document> and one <toc>. In lenient mode a later
// one's attributes override the earlier one's and the attributes it does not
// set are kept.
//
// <toc/> turns on the table of contents (Creator.AddTOC), which lists the
// chapters and is placed before them when the document is written, wherever
// the tag sits. heading sets its heading text, styled with heading-font,
// heading-font-size and heading-color. font, font-size and color style the
// lines, separator sets the leader text between title and page number,
// level-offset the indent per chapter level, line-margin the line margins and
// show-links whether lines link to their chapters. Lines of chapters drawn
// before the tag are restyled too. The tag takes no child elements.
//
// <header> and <footer> hold content drawn on every page, in a block the width
// of the page and the height of the top or bottom page margin. Their content
// nests as in a Block, so a <division> lays out several components one after
// the other, and they may carry typography (font, font-size, color, ...) to it.
// They are executed again for every page with the data passed to
// RenderTemplate, so they can call the page helpers: pageNum returns the page
// number, totalPages the page count, and chapter the *ChapterInfo of the
