// ParsedTemplate is a template read and compiled once that can be rendered many
// times, into different creators, with different data. Compiling (reading the
// source, compiling the text/template and its subtemplates, and installing the
// escaping helpers) is done up front by ParseTemplate; a creator's RenderTemplate
// or ValidateTemplate (or the Block equivalents) executes the compiled template
// with the caller's data and builds the resulting XML tree, so the read and
// compile cost is not paid per render. A parsed template is not bound to a
// creator and may be reused across documents.
//
// Fonts referenced by a path are loaded per render (once per RenderTemplate
// call), so the same font is embedded independently in each document.
//
// A parsed template is safe for concurrent RenderTemplate and ValidateTemplate
// calls (and the Block equivalents) into different creators: text/template's
// Execute may run in parallel, and every render gets its own processor state
// and font cache. Rendering into the same creator or block from several
// goroutines at once is not safe.
//
// The values in TemplateOptions are shared by every render:
//   - A model.PdfFont in FontMap is not safe to write into several documents at
//     once. Load fonts with `path('...')` or use a ParsedTemplate per goroutine
//     with its own fonts.
//   - A gradient color in ColorMap is modified while it is drawn. Write
//     gradients inline in the template or use a ParsedTemplate per goroutine.
//   - A ChartMap chart is drawn by every render, so it must be safe for
//     concurrent Render calls. A shared ImageMap image is safe.
//   - HelperFuncMap functions are called by several renders at once, so a
//     helper that keeps state must synchronize it.
type ParsedTemplate struct{_baged *TemplateOptions ;_becab *_cc .Template ;_aaafc string ;_bfaegc []templatePagePart ;};

